(O108 - Probe Single Axis X)
(Probes X in one direction, sets work offset)
(Requires: [PROBE] VEL, SEARCH_DIST, XY_CLEARANCE, Z_DROP, DIAMETER in LinuxCNC INI)
(Usage: Position near X edge, then call)

O108 sub

    #<probe_vel> = #<_ini[PROBE]VEL>
    #<search_dist> = #<_ini[PROBE]SEARCH_DIST>
    #<xy_clear> = #<_ini[PROBE]XY_CLEARANCE>
    #<z_drop> = #<_ini[PROBE]Z_DROP>
    #<probe_diam> = #<_ini[PROBE]DIAMETER>

    M5
    M9
    G90
    G40
    G49

    (Drop to probe height)
    G91
    G0 Z-#<z_drop>

    (Probe X- direction)
    G38.2 X-#<search_dist> F#<probe_vel>
    #<x1> = #5061

    (Retract)
    G0 X#<xy_clear>
    G0 Z#<z_drop>

    (Set work offset, accounting for probe radius)
    #<radius> = [#<probe_diam> / 2.0]
    G10 L20 P0 X[#<x1> + #<radius>]

    G90

    (MSG, X edge set: X#<x1>)

O108 endsub
M2
